language ESSENCE' 1.0

$ Regression for #1227; both original quasigroup fixtures use this instance.
$ There are exactly two solutions. Sorting matrix values hid misplaced entries.
letting n be 4
letting mat be [
    [0, 1, 0, 0],
    [0, 0, 2, 0],
    [0, 3, 0, 0],
    [0, 0, 0, 4]
]

find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..n)
such that
    (forAll i,j : int(1..n) . (0 < mat[i,j]) -> (x[i,j] = mat[i,j])),
    (forAll i : int(1..n) . (allDiff(x[i,..]) /\ allDiff(x[..,i])))
